# NeferWL screen-capture allowlist example.
#
# Without /etc/neferwl/capture-allow, NeferWL allows these executables to
# capture the screen (the built-in list):
#
#   /usr/bin/grim
#   /usr/bin/nefercap
#   /usr/lib/xdg-desktop-portal-wlr
#   /usr/libexec/xdg-desktop-portal-wlr
#
# To allow a tool installed elsewhere, copy this file to
# /etc/neferwl/capture-allow as root and add its path. The file REPLACES the
# built-in list entirely, so keep the entries you still need.
#
# Format: one absolute executable path per line, the resolved path that
# /proc/<pid>/exe shows (a symlink is never followed). Blank lines and lines
# starting with '#' are ignored. A line with only '*' disables the check:
# every client may capture. An invalid file (a relative path, anything that is
# not a path) lets no client capture, and the log names the line.
# NeferWL reads the file at startup and again whenever it changes.
#
# The file and every directory down from / must be root-owned, not group- or
# other-writable, and not symlinks; otherwise no client may capture.
# See docs/capture.md.
#
# Never list an interpreter (python, bash, node...): every script it runs
# would then be allowed to capture.
/usr/bin/grim
/usr/bin/nefercap
/usr/lib/xdg-desktop-portal-wlr
/usr/libexec/xdg-desktop-portal-wlr
